<title>BELGIUM: CREDIT COMMUNAL/GEMEENTEKREDIET CUTS SAVINGS RATES.</title>
<headline>CREDIT COMMUNAL/GEMEENTEKREDIET CUTS SAVINGS RATES.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian bank Credit Communal/</p>
<p>Gemeentekrediet said on Thursday it would lower the interest</p>
<p>rate offered on its three- and five-year savings, or &quot;cash&quot;</p>
<p>bonds, effective Friday.</p>
<p>The changes are as follows (old rates in brackets):</p>
<p>    Three-year   3.65% (3.80%)</p>
<p>    Five-year    4.60% (4.70%)</p>
<p>The rate offered on one-year bonds would remain unchanged at</p>
<p>2.80 percent, the bank said.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
